        "Content": "This beautifully restored old stone cottage seamlessly blends timeless character with contemporary comfort, having been thoughtfully extended and renovated throughout to an exceptional standard. Occupying a superb south-facing position on the Shore Road in Querrin, the property enjoys uninterrupted views across the magnificent Shannon Estuary, offering a peaceful coastal setting in one of West Clare's most picturesque locations.\r\n\r\nQuerrin is a charming rural village nestled between the popular seaside towns of Kilrush and Kilkee, with both towns just a short drive away, providing an excellent range of shops, schools, cafés, restaurants, and everyday amenities. The surrounding coastline, quiet country roads, and nearby beaches make this an ideal location for those seeking a tranquil lifestyle while remaining well connected.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation has been designed with modern family living in mind while retaining the warmth and character of the original cottage. It comprises a welcoming kitchen, a comfortable living room, utility room, family bathroom, and four well-proportioned bedrooms, including a spacious principal bedroom with en-suite.\r\n\r\nTo the rear, the property enjoys a generous private garden offering ample space for outdoor entertaining, gardening, or family recreation. A substantial detached garage provides excellent storage and is perfectly suited for use as a workshop, hobby space, or additional workspace.\r\n\r\nWith its enviable south-facing aspect overlooking the shore, high-quality finish throughout, and stunning estuary views, this is a rare opportunity to acquire a turnkey home in an idyllic coastal setting. Whether as a permanent residence, holiday home, or investment property, this exceptional home offers the perfect balance of traditional charm, modern convenience, and breathtaking natural surroundings."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hall: (2.1 x 5.9) Tiled floor\r\nKitchen: (5.9 x 3.2) Tiled floor, wall and base units, solid fuel stove with back boiler, hob, cooker, integrated fridge/freezer\r\nUtility: (1.8 x 2.2) Tiled floor, wall units, plumbed for w/m\r\nBathroom: (2.1 x 2.0) Fully tiled, bath, shower, wc, whb\r\nBedroom 1: (4.4 x 3.2) Carpet, timber ceiling, fitted wardrobes\r\nBedroom 2: (4.0 x 5.0) Timber floor, curtains, fitted wardrobes\r\nBedroom 3: (3.3 x 2.3) Timber floor, velux window\r\nBedroom 4: (2.6 x 3.3) Timber floor"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tBeautiful old stone cottage that has been restored and blends timeless character.\r\n•\tMagnificent uninterrupted views of the Shannon Estuary which provide a peaceful setting of one of West Clare's picturesque locations.\r\n•\tDesigned for modern family living.\r\n•\tPrivate garden to the rear.\r\n•\tDetached garage which provides excellent storage and can also be used as a workshop or hobby space.\r\n•\tRare opportunity to acquire a turnkey home in an idyllic coastal setting\r\n•\tBER D1 247.86 kWh/m²/yr. No: 119369882"
